Disable VS Code forwarded-ports features via remoteExplorer.ts

This patch now ONLY handles the VS Code side of proxy/ports disabling. The
code-server proxy-route disabling has been moved out of this patch and applied
directly to the code-server source files (see "code-server source changes"
below) as commented-out dead code for an easy re-enable path.

VS Code change (remoteExplorer.ts):

- enableForwardedPortsFeatures() sets featuresEnabled / viewEnabled to false,
  so the Ports (Forwarded Ports) view is never registered and
  portsFeaturesEnabled stays at its default Disabled.
- Because portsFeaturesEnabled is never AdditionalFeatures, both the process
  port scanner (extHostTunnelService $registerCandidateFinder) and the
  terminal-output scanner (OutputAutomaticPortForwarding) become no-ops, so
  no "new port available" popup appears and nothing is forwarded.

Note: The tunnelView.ts "Forward a Port" command and CommandPalette entries are
NOT commented out in this patch; they are disabled by the later
disable-debug-console-ports.diff patch which wraps the entire tunnelView
commands section in an if(false) block. When applied alone, this patch relies
on remoteExplorer.ts to prevent the Ports view from being registered, which
makes the ForwardPortAction commands unreachable through the UI.

code-server source changes (NO LONGER in this patch; now live in source):

The proxy route disabling is done directly in the code-server source by
commenting out the implementation (kept as dead code for an easy re-enable):

- src/node/proxy.ts             createProxyServer() + error/proxyReq/proxyRes
                                event handlers commented out
- src/node/routes/domainProxy.ts domain-based proxy router/wsRouter middleware
                                bodies (proxy.web / proxy.ws) commented out
- src/node/routes/index.ts      /proxy/:port and /absproxy/:port route
                                registration + domainProxy/pathProxy imports
                                commented out (also the WebsocketRequest type
                                import, no longer used)
- src/node/routes/pathProxy.ts  getProxyTarget() + _proxy.web / _proxy.ws calls
                                commented out (no callers left)

With those source edits applied (in the source tree, not via this patch):
- /proxy/:port and /absproxy/:port routes are not registered, so requests fall
  through to the 404 catch-all in routes/index.ts (NOT 403).
- createProxyServer() in src/node/proxy.ts is not invoked, so the http-proxy
  instance and its event handlers are not created.
- ensureProxyEnabled() / proxyEnabled() in http.ts are left intact as dead code.

The proxy-uri.diff patch is still independent and still injects
VSCODE_PROXY_URI into terminals, but following those URLs now returns 404.

To verify (VS Code part):
1. Apply: quilt push disable-proxy.diff
2. Start: code-server --auth none
3. Open the Command Palette - "Forward a Port" is unreachable (Ports view is
   not registered).
4. Re-enable VS Code part: quilt pop disable-proxy.diff

To verify (code-server source part, now independent of this patch):
1. Start: code-server --auth none
2. curl -i http://localhost:8080/proxy/3000/
   Expected: 404 Not Found (handled by the source edits, not this patch).

